The 2027 edition of BBC Radio 1’s Big Weekend will take place in Brighton next summer.

Past years have seen the broadcaster’s flagship festival bring Lana Del Rey to Hull, Taylor Swift perform in Norwich, Sabrina Carpenter headline in Luton, Ed Sheeran take the stage in Coventry and more. Earlier this summer, Zara Larsson and Olivia Dean headlined the 2026 edition , which took place in Herrington Country Park in Sunderland.

### 🎤 Key Highlights & Community Reactions

This morning (Thursday November 26) Greg James revealed on Radio 1 Breakfast that the 2027 edition will be held at Preston Park in Brighton between May 28 and 30.

“If Radio 1 was a place, it would be Brighton. It’s got an amazing musical heritage, loves bringing different people together and wants to make sure fun is prioritised,” he shared. “It’s actually stupid that it’s taken so long for us to do a Big Weekend there. Sorry about that.”

The BBC are working alongside Brighton & Hove City Council to host the 80,000 capacity festival, and ensuring that it is as safe and inclusive as possible for guests.

“Radio 1’s Big Weekend is a huge part of what we do as a station, celebrating the very best of music and giving audiences the chance to see some of the most exciting and talked-about artists live on their doorstep, alongside discovering new and emerging talent,” shared Aled Haydn Jones, Head of Radio 1. “We’re really excited to be taking the festival to Brighton in 2027 and can’t wait for another brilliant weekend.”

Bella Sankey, Brighton & Hove City Council Leader, said: “Brighton & Hove has an incredible music and cultural scene, so we’re a perfect home for Radio 1’s Big Weekend. It will bring some of the biggest names in music, along with thousands of fans, providing a real showcase for the city and a boost for local businesses.

